[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` exactly as given (no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`, therefore
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **`-O0`**), gcc 11.5.0, x86-64, glibc. `c_src/` was not modified.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Everything below drives **both** shared objects through `dlopen`/`dlsym` only —
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `array`, `perform_expensive_operations`, `long_exec`. No Rust function is called
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m directly anywhere in the test suite, so the `#[no_mangle]` wrappers and the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m exported `.bss` object are themselves under test.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## What the library is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 68 lines, one translation unit. `f(x)` is the inner loop body
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m x = x * 3 + 7;  x = x ^ (x >> 3);  x = x - (x << 1);  x = x / 2 + x % 7;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `perform_expensive_operations()` applies `f^100` to each of 262144 `int`s in the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m exported global `array`. `long_exec(seed)` does `srand(seed)`, fills the array
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m with `rand()`, calls `perform_expensive_operations()` 2000 times, and prints the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m XOR of the result with `printf("%d\n", …)`. One `long_exec` is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2000 × 100 × 262144 ≈ 5.2·10^10 applications of `f`, ~470 s of CPU at `-O0`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The Rust translation reproduces `perform_expensive_operations` literally, but
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `long_exec` does **not** run the nested loop: `src/fast.rs` computes the same
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `f^200000` by exact function-iteration algebra (Brent cycle finding + a memo of
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m "how this value relates to its cycle"), which is why the Rust `long_exec` takes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 0.4 s instead of 470 s. That accelerator is the whole risk surface of this
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m translation, and most of the effort below is aimed at it.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Phase A — surface map
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | artifact | content |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |----------|---------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `SYMBOLS.md` | `nm -D` on both objects; 3 C symbols, all exported by Rust; `array` 0x100000 bytes on both sides; 0 missing, 0 undefined non-libc |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `ERRORS.md` | 20 rows. The greps establish the C has **no** error codes, sentinels, asserts, null checks or range checks, so the rejection surface is the implicit numeric edge conditions (signed overflow, negative shifts, truncating division, sign-of-dividend remainder, seed extremes). Rows 14/15/19/20 are recorded as unreachable/not-applicable with the reason. |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `CONFIGS.md` | 40 rows. The C has no runtime options at all, so the axes are: entry point, `k` = number of `perform_expensive_operations` calls, array data shape, and `seed`. |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m No C source was left untranslated — `c_src` has exactly one `.c` file, and every
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m non-`static` definition in it has a Rust counterpart.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Phase B — valid-path results
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | what | scale | result |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |------|-------|--------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `perform_expensive_operations` (`f^100`), **exhaustive** | all 2^32 `int` values, as 16384 disjoint 262144-wide windows, whole-array checksum compared | **0 mismatches** (`tools/sweep.sh`, 24 shards, all `DONE`) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `perform_expensive_operations` composed, `k = 0 … 83` | 24 rows × 262144 values: zeros, all-ones, all `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX`, 37-value sentinel tile, three contiguous windows (around 0, at `INT_MIN`, at `INT_MAX`), 6 random fills, sparse, values already on cycles of `f`, `k=0` no-op, state carry-over, randomized `seed × k` matrix | all byte-identical |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `long_exec` end-to-end | **42 seeds**, full C runs (~470 s CPU each, run in parallel): exact `printf` bytes **and** the full 1 MiB final array compared with `cmp` | all identical |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | accelerated vs. naive through the FFI | `srand(s)` + `rand()` fill + 2000 naive `pxo` calls vs. `long_exec(s)`, for 9 seeds; and the same naive route on the **C** library for seed 42 | all identical |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | stream parity | C writes nothing to stderr; default-feature Rust matches on both fds | identical |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The exhaustive sweep is the load-bearing result: it makes the Rust `f^100`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m provably equal to the C `f^100` on the entire input domain, so every composition
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `f^(100k)` agrees too. The accelerated-vs-naive checks then pin `src/fast.rs` to
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m that same composition, and the 42 direct C runs confirm the whole pipeline
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m end to end.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Negative controls were run to confirm the harness can actually fail: the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m checksum comparison distinguishes `pxo:1` from `pxo:2`, and the test suite caught
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m three real problems during development (a wrong `dlsym` idiom for the data
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     63[0m:[38;5;10m[49m symbol, a reference-fixture mix-up, and the stderr difference introduced by the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     64[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `debug-stats` feature).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     65[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     66[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Incidental finding from the accelerator's own diagnostics (`--features
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     67[0m:[38;5;10m[49m debug-stats`): a `long_exec` run resolves into 7–9 distinct cycles of `f`, of
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     68[0m:[38;5;10m[49m lengths `[25, 47, 84, 109, 126, 631, 3166, 11991, 52330]`, with ~1.7 M memo
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     69[0m:[38;5;10m[49m entries. The final image contains only ~62 k distinct values.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     70[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     71[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Phase C — error-path results
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     72[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     73[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The C library has no error surface to compare, which the table documents
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     74[0m:[38;5;10m[49m mechanically rather than assuming. Every row that *is* reachable has a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     75[0m:[38;5;10m[49m differential test in `tests/errors.rs` (14 tests, all passing):
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     76[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * signed-overflow bands around `INT_MIN`, `INT_MIN/2`, `INT_MIN/3`, `INT_MAX/3`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     78[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `INT_MAX/2`, `INT_MAX` (±3 each);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     79[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * negative arithmetic right shift and negative left shift (all of `-64..0` plus
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     80[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `INT_MIN`, `INT_MIN+1`, `INT_MIN+7`, `-2^30`, `-2^20`);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     81[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * division truncation toward zero and remainder sign, over `-70..=70`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     82[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (every residue class mod 2 and mod 7, both signs);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     83[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `INT_MIN / 2` does not trap, and `INT_MIN / -1` is unreachable because both
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     84[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   divisors are literals;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     85[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * seed boundary sweep across the FFI: `0, 1, 2, INT_MAX, INT_MAX+1, 32767/32768,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     86[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   65535/65536, 2147483646, UINT_MAX-1, UINT_MAX`, plus `-1 as u32`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     87[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `INT_MIN as u32`, and 64-bit values truncated to 32 bits, requiring equal bit
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     88[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   patterns to give equal output;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     89[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `k = 0` leaves the array bit-unchanged in both libraries;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     90[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * pristine `.bss`: both `array` objects are all-zero at load, in a dedicated
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     91[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   test binary that owns a fresh process (`tests/bss_initial.rs`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     92[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     93[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Two documented findings rather than assumptions:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     94[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     95[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `srand(0)` aliases `srand(1)` in glibc, so seeds 0 and 1 produce identical
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     96[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   output — confirmed on the C side from its own reference dumps.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     97[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * A negative printed value is **unreachable**: after `f^200000` every element
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     98[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   lies in `[-1073734582, -536871525]`, so all 262144 elements have bit 31 set
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     99[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   and the even count cancels it. `%d` vs. `%u` is therefore not observable
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    100[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   through this API. `ERRORS.md` row 18 records this instead of claiming a test
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    101[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   for a case that cannot occur.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    102[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    103[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Phase D — symbol parity and feature combinations
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    104[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    105[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `[features]` declares exactly one optional feature and no defaults, so the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    106[0m:[38;5;10m[49m complete power set is `{}` and `{debug-stats}`. `tools/check_features.sh`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    107[0m:[38;5;10m[49m enumerates it from `Cargo.toml` (not hard-coded), and for each combination
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    108[0m:[38;5;10m[49m rebuilds the `cdylib` into its own target directory, re-checks `nm -D` parity and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    109[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the `array` object size, and runs the whole suite against *that* build.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    110[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
